        language: "python",
        description: "Master list comprehensions, dictionary operations, and algorithmic efficiency. Maps CSN CS 138 (Python for Data Science) and UNLV CS 135/202 to the official PCEP (Python Certified Entry-Level Programmer) exam.",
        overviewNote: "Click line numbers to inspect Python memory model, data structures, and algorithmic complexity.",
        takeaways: [
          "Fulfills <strong>CSN CS 138</strong> & <strong>UNLV CS 135</strong> lower-division programming requirement.",
          "Covers PCEP certification exam domains: Data Types, Control Flow, Collections, and Exception Handling.",
          "Prepares for upper-division Data Structures (UNLV CS 302) by building clean algorithmic patterns."
